(6511854, 967290, 86218, '<td valign="top">A very cute capture and like your notes say, patience did pay off getting this pose. Being in the Kruger obviously limited you to the angles you could get. The single biggest handicap for any photographer... sitting in a car. You did well to get this pose and angle on it. Congrats</td>', 'A very cute capture and like your notes say, patience did pay off getting this pose. Being in the Kruger obviously limited you to the angles you could get. The single biggest handicap for any photographer... sitting in a car. You did well to get this pose and angle on it. Congrats', '2011-08-22 07:17:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6511855, 967381, 108069, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top 10! Wonderful portrait.</td>', 'Congrats on the top 10! Wonderful portrait.', '2011-08-22 07:25:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6511863, 967118, 135479, '<td valign="top">To be honest this was quickly setup and shot due to the deadline. I was very limited for space to shoot this as the room was cramped, the idea was to show all the vertical lines meeting together such as the floor, the wallpaper, panelling, the woman, the legs, the seams in the stockings. The hand bag is there to break the vertical lines and to give part of the story of the scene, who is she, is she coming or going, whats is she looking at on the wall... but it only deserved a rating of: 6.0682</td>', 'To be honest this was quickly setup and shot due to the deadline. I was very limited for space to shoot this as the room was cramped, the idea was to show all the vertical lines meeting together such as the floor, the wallpaper, panelling, the woman, the legs, the seams in the stockings. The hand bag is there to break the vertical lines and to give part of the story of the scene, who is she, is she coming or going, whats is she looking at on the wall... but it only deserved a rating of: 6.0682', '2011-08-22 07:54:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6511864, 966655, 14476, '<td valign="top">Super imagination, Karen.  Congratulations.</td>', 'Super imagination, Karen.  Congratulations.', '2011-08-22 08:04:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6511869, 966757, 64670, '<td valign="top">BRILLIANT!  It''s always wonderful to see you on the front page, but this one especially because it''s so NOT what I''d normally think the voters would appreciate - AWESOME!</td>', 'BRILLIANT!  It''s always wonderful to see you on the front page, but this one especially because it''s so NOT what I''d normally think the voters would appreciate - AWESOME!', '2011-08-22 08:14:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6511871, 967158, 117474, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i>The commenters who noted the narrow DOF would be the first to complain about the lack of bokeh in the background... if the DOF was deeper.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I reckon had the DOF been wider you could have blurred the background artificially in PP legally (I did it in an entry of mine in an advanced challenge recently and my image was validated). That''d leave the tiger in good focus and the background happily boring :-) <br/>Just a thought. Nice image. I love tigers. They''re not afraid of water like lions, so they''re masters of the land! I sort of see what tanguera meant about hugging them. Apparently you can train them into submission by flicking drops water from your fingers in their face from a young age. I don''t know if I believe that or not, but if you could manage it while hugging them you might get away with it :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by hahn23:The commenters who noted the narrow DOF would be the first to complain about the lack of bokeh in the background... if the DOF was deeper. I reckon had the DOF been wider you could have blurred the background artificially in PP legally (I did it in an entry of mine in an advanced challenge recently and my image was validated). That''d leave the tiger in good focus and the background happily boring :-) Just a thought. Nice image. I love tigers. They''re not afraid of water like lions, so they''re masters of the land! I sort of see what tanguera meant about hugging them. Apparently you can train them into submission by flicking drops water from your fingers in their face from a young age. I don''t know if I believe that or not, but if you could manage it while hugging them you might get away with it :-)', '2011-08-22 08:17:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6511873, 967211, 119747, '<td valign="top">Keep this up for Longshots! ;-)</td>', 'Keep this up for Longshots! ;-)', '2011-08-22 08:21:04.000000', NULL, 0),
